WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.540
STEPHEN GREENBLATT: Shakespeare's Othello opens in Venice,

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.570
where we're standing now.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:11.970
It opens in the darkness, under the windows

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:18.570
of a house, where Iago and Roderigo are trying to stir up trouble

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:24.090
by telling the master of the house, the important senator, Brabanzio,

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.390
that his daughter has eloped with a Moor.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.650
They start shouting up in the darkness, thieves!

00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:35.219
Iago says, make it sound like there's a fire in the populous city,

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:35.760
and so forth.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:42.030
And Brabanzio comes and says indignantly, this is Venice!

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:44.354
My house is not a grange.

00:00:44.354 --> 00:00:46.020
I'm not in the country, in a farm house.

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.980
This is Venice, he says.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:51.570
It's a way of not simply of telling the audience where the play is located,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:54.510
but saying something about the nature of the city--

00:00:54.510 --> 00:01:00.510
its power, its security, its grandeur, the absence of threat,

00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:02.730
the ridiculousness of trying to frighten him.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:07.320
And then he learns that he should indeed, as a father, be frightened.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.820
His daughter has eloped.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:15.000
And not only has she eloped, she's eloped with the Moor, Othello,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.930
someone that Brabanzio, the senator, had invited to his house

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.460
to tell the story of his life.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:27.750
And there, Othello and the senator's only child, his daughter, Desdemona,

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:32.070
have made their acquaintance, which has developed into a love,

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:35.070
and which has now led to her elopement.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.590
That's the opening situation.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:42.780
Brabanzio, the father, outraged, says he will rush off

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:47.610
to the doge of Venice, the duke, the ruler of the whole republic,

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:48.750
the senior figure.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.220
And he'll demand legal satisfaction, the annulment, in effect, of the marriage.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.560
And he declares that he has the kind of power to do this.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:58.680
He's one of the most powerful figures--

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.480
Brabanzio-- in the city.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.460
Venice was an oligarchy.

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.640
That's to say, it was ruled by a small number of noblemen.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:07.590
And Brabanzio is one of them.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:13.470
So he goes off, confident that his complaint will be heard.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:14.520
Where does he go?

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.540
He goes to find the duke in the duke's palace, the doge's palace.

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.410
And that's where we are, at the moment, in front

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.130
of the great Ducal Palace in Venice.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:31.560
Now, it happens that we also learn that Brabanzio is not the only one rushing

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.880
off to the Ducal Palace.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:39.570
They have sent messages from the Ducal Palace trying to find Othello.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:43.590
Why are they trying to find Othello, who is in fact, at that moment,

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.680
in an inn with his bride, Desdemona?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.090
They're trying to find him because there's a political crisis.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:54.060
On the one hand, we have Venice, the city,

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.310
in all of its grandeur and security.

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.940
On the other hand, we have a threatened empire.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.370
Venice was a very powerful republic.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:06.990
It controlled territory, not only in its immediate surroundings,

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:14.910
but throughout the Mediterranean, as far east as the eastern Mediterranean,

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:17.070
places like Rhodes and Cyprus.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:18.900
And there's a crisis--

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:24.270
a crisis with the people at the outer edge of Venetian power,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.660
namely the other great power in the Mediterranean,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:33.390
the Turks, the Muslim power under the Turkish sultan.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:38.070
The background of Shakespeare's tragedy is

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:45.540
what happens at the outer edge of a great empire, when the forces of Venice

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.930
have to meet and encounter the forces of the enemy Turk.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:04:00.660
For that encounter, Venice relies on its navy and on its military leaders.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:05.520
Those military leaders were not, by any means, always Venetians.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.410
On the contrary, for the most part, they were people from outside of Venice,

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:15.810
hired by the Venetians especially to conduct their battles.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:18.480
In Venice, there are very, very few statues

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.120
of Venetian-born military leaders.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:24.840
The greatest statue in Venice of a military leader

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:29.540
is of Bartolomeo Colleoni, a great condottiero

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:32.160
as they call it, a great military commander.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.890
And that statue is a celebration of a man

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:42.060
who was from Bergamo, a different city in Italy, hired by the Venetians

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.440
to lead its forces.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:48.510
And that's the situation we find at the beginning of Othello,

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.510
when we enter the rooms in the doge's palace,

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:56.190
find the Venetian senators anxiously talking to each other about the threat

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:59.190
out at the edge of their empire, in Cyprus.

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:03.350
That's the situation that is evoked at the beginning of Othello,

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.560
in which the Venetian senate tries to decide whom it should

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:10.040
send to command its garrison in Cyprus.

00:05:10.040 --> 00:05:15.170
The Venetians are powerful, one of the most powerful states in Europe.

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:16.280
They have a great city.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.080
They have wealth.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:19.520
They have confidence.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:23.060
But they need military power, and their military power

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:27.230
depends upon foreigners-- foreigners like Othello;

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:31.070
like the character of Marcus Luccicos, who seems to have a Greek name

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:36.290
and is in Florence; like the Florentine Cassio; like Iago,

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:38.540
who has a Spanish name.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:42.770
Virtually all of the Venetian military figures

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:48.210
appear to be foreigners, mercenaries in the employment of Venice.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:53.090
So on the one hand, we have a tight, cozy, wealthy, confident oligarchy

00:05:53.090 --> 00:05:53.990
in Venice.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:58.880
On the other hand, we have military leaders who are from outside of Venice,

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.530
and who help the Venetians oppose their deep enemies,

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:06.560
their frightening enemies, the Turks, the Muslim forces.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:12.380
And all of that works more or less fine, until we

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:17.570
have the critical moment that's depicted in the play, in which one

00:06:17.570 --> 00:06:21.380
of these outsiders, namely Othello, gets alarmingly

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:26.900
close to the center of Venice, namely the daughter of one of the leading

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:31.310
senators of the city, Brabanzio's daughter, Desdemona.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:36.800
And at that moment, the outsiders in the employment of Venice

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:40.220
suddenly seem as frightening or more frightening

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:45.040
than the enemy Turks out there at the edge of the republic.

